  "arithmetic_terminal": "ImbalancedChen.Part3.FixedMarkTail.physical_twisted_summable",
  "quantifiers": [
    "m is a fixed nonzero integer; any integer second frequency, including zero, and any unit on the first frequency may vary independently with d.",
    "For delta<1/4 the nonnegative arithmetic price sums. A positive 0<delta<1/4 gives a D^(-delta) tail for D>=1 in the untilted series.",
    "The physical assertion is for z,m,h>0 and positive d coprime to z, C=d sqrt(z). Arithmetic is independent of z; the geometric constant contains sqrt(mh)/z."
  ],
  "mathematical_proof": [
    "Two-frequency fourth moment and inversion-graph counting at prime moduli, unit-dilation orbit for the fixed frequency.",
    "Literal CRT twists of both marks, proved unit scaling and the triangle estimate for every prime power of exponent at least two.",
    "Positive finite smooth-number Euler products and summable local envelopes, with only finitely many bad exponent-one primes.",
    "Realized cuspOneMatrixSum, its phase, inverseResidue at the same modulus, original generalJ symmetric integral at order one."
  ],
  "withheld": [
    "Composite-modulus pointwise 3/4 estimate, Weil or stationary phase.",
    "General-cusp group decomposition, the full weight-two limiting operation, physical Petersson/Hilbert identification, Kuznetsov inversion or distribution saving."
  ],
